  "title": "TCP Stream: Make better decision about which side is the server",
  "description": "The TCP Stream tap, upon encountering the first packet for a stream,\nhas to decide which side is the server and will be shown as the source\nside intially. (\"Switch Directions\" is used to swap.)\n\nCurrently the assumption is that the first packet from a stream is\nthe SYN packet, so the destination is the server. Check to see if\nthe first packet is a SYN packet (server is dest) or SYN-ACK packet\n(server is source), and fall back to assuming that the lower numbered\nport is the server in the remaining cases. This makes it more likely\nthat the graph shown initially is the server graph as intended.\n\nRelated to #10722",
